# Markdown lifecycle status

## Allowed markdown statuses

Markdown docs use `doc_status` with these values only:

- `draft`: incomplete or unverified
- `ready`: reviewed and aligned with current Figma/tokens
- `needs-review`: previously valid but potentially stale after upstream changes

## Required status metadata

- Lifecycle status values are defined in this rule and enforced by the docs pipeline.
- Component docs (`docs/components/*.md`, excluding `overview.md`) must carry an explicit lifecycle status in the pipeline metadata.
- Overview/foundation/workflow pages should also carry lifecycle status when edited.

## YAML alignment note

- Component specs keep `status` limited to `draft | ready` (as defined in `component-spec-yaml.mdc`).
- `needs-review` is markdown-only and should be used when docs may be stale but YAML has not been revalidated yet.

## Transition guidance

- Set to `needs-review` after major Figma component changes, token renames, or render-layout regressions.
- Promote to `ready` only after re-checking source Figma and token mappings.

Automatic drift trigger (component docs):

- required lifecycle metadata is missing or invalid.

## `ready` hard gate (components)

For component pages (`docs/components/*.md`, excluding `overview.md`), `ready` requires all:

- Linked spec status is also `ready`.
- No `TBD` markers remain in markdown content.
- `figma.last_verified` is concrete (not missing/`TBD`).
- No unresolved rows (`open` or `accepted`) in `## Design–Token Discrepancies`.
- `## Overview` includes a `### Visual Proof` subsection with a concrete screenshot URL (not `TBD`).
